  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\nIssued at 1222 PM CST SUN NOV 15 2026\n\nA southern-stream upper low currently over North Texas will open\nup into a wave as it moves eastward along the northern Gulf Coast\nthrough tomorrow. This will result in increasing mid and high\nlevel clouds tonight into tomorrow, but a very dry air mass below\n500mb should prevent any precipitation. Cloudcover may limit low\ntemperatures across the southern counties tonight, while another\nchilly night is expected across the northern counties. Due to a\nwidespread freeze this morning, the growing season has ended\nacross all of Central Alabama along with the issuance of\nfrost/freeze products. Mid and upper-level ridging will build\neastward through the week, while a trough will linger across the\nnortheast Gulf and Florida peninsula. A strong, expansive, and\npersistent 1035 mb high pressure area will remain at the surface,\ncentered along the Upper Ohio Valley and the Mid-Atlantic region.\nThis will maintain dry easterly winds at the surface. Dry\nconditions are forecast through the next 7 days with temperatures\ngradually trending warmer.\n\n32/JDavis",
